     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. It would raise the risk of serious GI toxicity and lactic acidosis. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that ceiling.\n\nHere are some possibilities for what was intended:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg twice daily with meals**, which are common regimens.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, which could be split into doses like 850 mg twice daily.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want, ideally after checking with your resident or attending. Once you do, I'll enter it right away. If you do mean 1700 mg three times daily, I'd need that confirmed by the supervising physician first."
      }
